3. Client-Server Communication with Serialization and Deserialization

Question: Write a TCP client-server program that serializes a student dictionary, sends it to the server, deserializes it, and returns a serialized response.

server3.py

import socket
import pickle
 
s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
s.bind(("localhost", 5002))
s.listen(1)
 
print("Server waiting...")
conn, addr = s.accept()
 
data = conn.recv(4096)
student = pickle.loads(data)  # Deserialize trusted data
print("Received data:", student)
 
reply = {"message": "Data received successfully"}
conn.send(pickle.dumps(reply))
 
conn.close()
s.close()

client3.py

import socket
import pickle
 
student = {
    "name": input("Enter name: "),
    "mark": int(input("Enter mark: "))
}
 
s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
s.connect(("localhost", 5002))
s.send(pickle.dumps(student))  # Serialize dictionary
 
reply = pickle.loads(s.recv(4096))
print("Server response:", reply)
 
s.close()

Sample Output

Enter name: Arun
Enter mark: 88
Server response: {'message': 'Data received successfully'}

Note: Only deserialize pickle data from trusted sources. This simple lab example assumes each serialized message fits in one recv() call.


