5. Token Ring Algorithm

Question: Simulate processes arranged in a ring. A single token circulates between processes, and only the process holding the token enters the critical section.

token_ring.py

import time
 
n = int(input("Enter number of processes: "))
 
if n <= 0:
    print("Number of processes must be positive")
else:
    token = 0
 
    for i in range(2 * n):
        print("Process", token, "has the token")
        print("Process", token, "enters critical section")
        print("Process", token, "exits critical section")
 
        token = (token + 1) % n
        print("Token passed to next process\\n")
        time.sleep(0.5)

Sample Output

Enter number of processes: 3
Process 0 has the token
Process 0 enters critical section
Process 0 exits critical section
Token passed to next process

Note: This is a single-program simulation of the token ring, not separate operating-system processes.


