7. Berkeley's Clock Synchronization Algorithm

Question: Implement a simplified Berkeley algorithm. A master gathers clock readings, calculates their average, and adjusts each clock to the average.

berkeley.py

clocks = [10, 20, 30, 40]
 
print("Original clock times:")
for i, t in enumerate(clocks):
    print("Clock", i, ":", t, "seconds")
 
average = sum(clocks) / len(clocks)
print("\\nMaster clock: Clock 0")
print("Average time:", average, "seconds")
 
print("\\nClock adjustments:")
for i in range(len(clocks)):
    adjustment = average - clocks[i]
    print("Clock", i, "adjustment:", adjustment)
    clocks[i] = average
 
print("\\nSynchronized clocks:")
for i, t in enumerate(clocks):
    print("Clock", i, ":", t, "seconds")

Sample Output

Original clock times:
Clock 0 : 10 seconds
Clock 1 : 20 seconds
Clock 2 : 30 seconds
Clock 3 : 40 seconds
Average time: 25.0 seconds
All synchronized clocks: 25.0 seconds

Note: This educational simulation ignores network delay and assumes equally reliable clock readings.


