8. Simulate Clock Drift Over One Minute

Question: Simulate two clocks starting at the same time. Clock B runs faster than Clock A by 10 milliseconds per second. Calculate the difference after one minute.

clock_drift.py

clock_a = 0.0
clock_b = 0.0
 
drift = 0.010  # 10 milliseconds per second
duration = 60
 
for i in range(duration):
    clock_a += 1.0
    clock_b += 1.0 + drift
 
difference = clock_b - clock_a
 
print("Clock A:", clock_a, "seconds")
print("Clock B:", round(clock_b, 3), "seconds")
print("Difference:", round(difference, 3), "seconds")
print("Difference in milliseconds:", round(difference * 1000, 1), "ms")

Sample Output

Clock A: 60.0 seconds
Clock B: 60.6 seconds
Difference: 0.6 seconds
Difference in milliseconds: 600.0 ms

Note: Drift = 10 ms/s × 60 s = 600 ms.


